course: dictionary
lesson: 4421
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The dictionary lists each meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is being used. Hammer can be a thing you hold, or an action you do. Read the words around it to decide.
explain: «Dad used a hammer to put a nail in the wall.» Here a hammer is a tool with a heavy metal head on a handle. Now read: «Rain hammered on the roof all night.» The rain is not holding a tool, so hammered must mean hit again and again.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you are probably right. If it sounds silly, try another meaning from the dictionary.
fact: A hammer is a tool with a heavy metal head on a handle, used for hitting nails into wood.
fact: As a verb, hammer means to hit something with a hammer, or to hit it hard again and again.
fact: In informal talk, to hammer someone means to beat them easily in a game.
fact: The hammer throw is a sport where a heavy metal ball on a wire is thrown.
fact: In woodwork, hold the nail carefully, keep your fingers clear, and wear goggles.
exercise: «Dad used a hammer to put a nail in the wall.» In this sentence, a hammer is | A small part inside the ear | A ball thrown in a sports event | A kind of food | *A tool with a heavy metal head on a handle
exercise: «Rain hammered on the roof all night.» What does hammered mean here? | Put away in a box | Melted slowly | Hung up to dry | *Hit again and again
exercise: Jay says, «We hammered them in the match!» What does he mean? | *We beat them easily | We played in the rain | We hit them with a tool | We lost by a lot
test: «An astronaut dropped a hammer and a feather on the Moon in 1971.» Here, hammer is a | *Noun, a tool | Verb, to hit hard | Verb, to beat someone | Noun, a sport
test: Which sport uses a hammer? | A card game played with a deck | A sport where a heavy metal ball on a wire is thrown | A race run on a track with hurdles | *A sport where a heavy metal ball on a wire is thrown, called the hammer throw
exam: In «a capuchin cracks a nut with a stone like a hammer», what job does the stone do? | It makes a loud sound like a monkey's call | *It works like a tool that hits, so it cracks the nut | It is used to dig a hole in the ground | It keeps the nut still while it is eaten
